
Methylation analysis

This directory contains downstream scripts used to process methylation results generated by Modkit.

Main script

pairwise_methylation_statistics.R

Processes methylation TSV files from two matched samples and:

applies the selected count_valid_m quality threshold;

matches the same TE-associated loci between samples;

calculates signed and absolute methylation-rate differences;

reports median and IQR values;

calculates the paired Hodges–Lehmann location-shift estimate with 95% confidence interval;

summarizes loci with absolute methylation differences of at least 5%, 10%, 15%, and 20%;

generates a table containing the 50 loci with the largest methylation differences.

The script can be used for both:

regional methylation
internal TE methylation

Plot generation is intentionally kept separate from this analysis script.

Example

Rscript pairwise_methylation_statistics.R \
    regional \
    sample_A.tsv \
    sample_B.tsv \
    results/pair_left \
    A \
    B \
    100

Output

*_paired_loci.tsv
*_summary.tsv
*_thresholds.tsv
*_top50.tsv

These tables are used for downstream result reporting and figure generation.
